# ===========================================
# Docker/ build context IS published (Dockerfiles, entrypoints, build context)
# so the community can build images and submit PRs. Two exclusions:
#
#  1. Link Guard (Pro engine) -- proprietary; never tracked, no matter what.
#  2. Ciphermail VENDOR ORIGINAL packages -- only repack-debs-nosystemd.sh
#     consumes them; the *generated* *-nosystemd.deb (what the Dockerfile
#     actually COPYs) IS tracked so contributors build without running repack.
#     Upstream source: https://gitlab.com/ciphermail/ciphermail-community-gateway
#     (see Docker/ciphermail/build/README.md). Maintainer keeps originals locally.
# ===========================================
/Docker/linkguard/
Docker/ciphermail/build/*_all.deb
Docker/ciphermail/build/data.tar.xz

# SpamAssassin Bayes corpus: runtime state, not shippable config (#292).
# Hermes previously shipped a pre-trained corpus built from unrelated mail,
# so every install scored against someone else's training. The directories
# must still exist because they are bind-mount sources, hence .gitkeep.
config/hermes/opt/hermes/sa-bayes/*
!config/hermes/opt/hermes/sa-bayes/.gitkeep
config/mail_filter/sa-bayes/*
!config/mail_filter/sa-bayes/.gitkeep
